---
import ContentLayout from '../../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';

const noSlash = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const u = (p: string) => `${noSlash}${p}`;
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Prototypes and MVPs in weeks | Freedom45"
  description="Test your idea with real users before the big spend. Freedom45 builds working prototypes and MVPs in weeks, using AI-first tools, for startups and public bodies."
  activePage="services"
>
  <header>
    <p class="eyebrow">Prototypes and MVPs</p>
    <h1>Find out if it works <span class="g">before you build it all.</span></h1>
    <p class="lead">The most expensive mistake in software is building the wrong thing well. A prototype puts the riskiest part of your idea in front of real users in weeks, so you spend on what works.</p>
  </header>

  <section>
    <h2>What you get</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>A working prototype,</b> not slides or wireframes: something people can actually use.</li>
      <li><b>Answers to the question that matters most:</b> will people use it, can it be built, what will it cost to do properly.</li>
      <li><b>A clear next step:</b> build it, change it, or stop with most of your budget still in hand.</li>
      <li><b>Code you own,</b> whichever you decide.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Who it's for</h2>
    <div class="cards cards--2">
      <div class="card"><h3>Founders</h3><p>Show investors and early customers something real, and learn what to build before you hire a team.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>Public bodies</h3><p>Test a new digital service with the people who'll use it, in Welsh and English where needed, before committing to a full build.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Why it's quick</h2>
    <p>We use AI-first tools heavily to get to a working version fast, and a person checks everything before it reaches you. You get speed without handing your product to a machine.</p>
  </section>

</ContentLayout>
